---
title: Chickpea Pot Pie
source: https://theeburgerdude.com/vegan-chicken-pot-pie/
author: ThreeBurgerDude
tags: [main course]
cuisine: American
---

Pre-heat the oven to 425 F.

== Filling

Dice @carrots{2 cups}, @celery{2 cups}, and @onion{2 cups}.

Place a #cast-iron skillet{} over medium heat and add @butter{1/2 cup}. Once melted, add diced vegetables and cook for ~{5 minutes}, stirring until softened.

Add minced @garlic{4 cloves}, @nutritional yeast{1 tbsp}, @fresh thyme{2 tsp}, @fresh sage{2 tsp}, @fresh rosemary{1 tsp}, @bay leaves{2}, and cook for another ~{1 minute}.

Stir in @flour{1/4 cup}, adding more butter if needed, and mix until combined.

Slowly add @vegetable broth{1 cup} and @milk{1 cup}, stirring until the mixture thickens.

Add @chickpeas{1 16-oz can}, drained and rinsed, and cook for ~{5 minutes} until heated through.

Remove from heat. Add @frozen peas{1 cup} and mix to combine.  Add @vegetable broth{1/2 cup} if the mixture is too thick. Season with @salt{to taste} and @black pepper{to taste}.

Remove bay leaves and rosemary sprigs.

== Assembly

Transfer the filling to a #baking dish{} and cover with @./puff-pastry{1 sheet}. Cut the pastry as desired to fit the dish and make a few slits to allow steam to escaope.

Brush the pastry with @milk{} and bake for ~{25 minutes}, until the pastry is browned and puffy.

Remove from the oven and let rest for ~{15 minutes} before serving.